WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.290
Your phone battery lasts a month. You rebuilt it... at breakfast.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.300
One new chip. One bent wire.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.420
Full signal in an elevator.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.790
Three floors underground. Phone companies would pay millions for that.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.110
And your tea... is still hot.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.640
Most people score around a hundred on an IQ test. Above one forty is rare.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.250
And most tests can't even measure past about one sixty.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.930
You? Five hundred.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.075
When did you put that there?

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:40.245
Last Tuesday. The new part comes today.

00:00:41.445 --> 00:00:47.055
Your body is totally normal. But your mind sees the answer... before anyone else sees the problem.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.430
So what's life like with five hundred? Amazing. And awful.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.600
Usually both at once.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.060
Plus: there are no hard puzzles left.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.090
Your sister's olympiad problem? A crossword.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.150
I've been stuck on that for three days!

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.470
Lucky guess.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.330
Minus: nothing excites you.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:19.090
Deep in your brain, dopamine cells fire hardest for good surprises. Things better than you expected.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.740
But you expect everything. So the spark never comes.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.560
Wow. Socks.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.380
You know every punchline in advance. So you laugh... a beat late. On purpose.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.480
You invent things, just for you.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.590
A mug that keeps tea at exactly sixty degrees Celsius.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:43.350
A lock that knows your walk. A wardrobe that folds your shirts.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.870
Leo! Your door hates me!

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.800
You walk like you're late.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:49.820
I am late!

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.060
The catch? You can never show the world.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.200
Show one mug, and tomorrow companies are lining up outside your door.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.030
So everything you build... stays home.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:07.930
You see the logic behind everything people do. So you pick the longest line... and get out first.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.410
Which is why people make no sense to you.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.150
They fight in lines. They pull doors that say push.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.730
They make the same mistake ten times.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:26.060
Imagine a sane man locked in an asylum for years. He copies everyone to fit in... until he forgets he's pretending.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:33.560
Every day, you play dumb to look normal. And deep down, you're scared that one day... it won't be an act.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.010
You see the weak spot in any system.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.640
Is my school's website safe?

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.490
Change your password.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:43.460
...Today?

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:44.160
Now.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.860
To you, every system is an open door. You only ever opened one. Your own.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.010
So you can't trust anything anymore.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:58.260
Everyone thinks the world is solid. Only you know how fragile it is.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.230
You could beat the stock market. Or crack a bank. Millionaire by next week.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:12.220
But every extra dollar you win... someone else loses. And you're not a thief.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.740
Besides, money brings attention.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.370
If you're so smart, why aren't you rich?

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.830
Because I'm smart.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.650
So you chose a quiet life. Invisible.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.540
Your test scores? Always one hundred. Exactly average.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.710
For you... that's the hard part.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.690
Your data? Quietly wiped from every list that sells people. Only yours.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.690
Nobody's looking for you. That's the real superpower.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.460
My Leo? He's an engineer. A good, normal boy.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.580
The price? Nobody knows who you really are.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.260
Not even your mom.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.740
So the smartest person alive lived the most ordinary life.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.940
And you'd have died of boredom... if not for one person.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.260
Your mom. Since the day Mia was born, she worked two jobs.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.300
And every month, she put a little aside.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.250
One account. One dream. Mia's university.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.660
She walked home to save the bus fare.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.210
She always gave you the last slice.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.120
She kept every drawing Mia ever made.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:36.700
None of it made sense. Other people's nonsense drove you crazy. Hers... you loved.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.210
Surprise party tonight. Don't tell her anything.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.780
I never tell anyone anything.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:55.540
Good afternoon. This is your bank's fraud team. Someone is emptying your account. Right now.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.660
What? No, no... that's my daughter's money!

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.210
Don't worry. We'll move it to a safe account. Stay on the line. Don't call anyone.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.520
Real banks never ask you to move money to a 'safe account'.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.070
But fear makes people fast. And he never let her hang up.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.180
You were at work across town. Even you can't predict what you can't see.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.550
Don't. Don't turn on the light.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:33.390
I'm so stupid. Seventeen years of Mia's money... and I just gave it away.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.530
Please. Don't tell Mia.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.745
Make a wish, Mom.

00:05:41.645 --> 00:05:44.275
I wish I could take today back.

00:05:45.775 --> 00:05:48.665
You could steal it all back in a minute. Ruin them all.

00:05:49.165 --> 00:05:50.855
But then you'd be just like them.

00:05:52.255 --> 00:05:55.355
You're not stupid, Mom. They're good at lies.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.805
I'm better at the truth.

00:06:02.405 --> 00:06:05.145
For the first time... you opened someone else's door.

00:06:06.145 --> 00:06:10.305
The number was fake. The account was real. You pulled that thread.

00:06:11.205 --> 00:06:17.075
Four minutes later: a basement on the edge of town. Forty phones. And a list.

00:06:17.875 --> 00:06:20.685
Three hundred names. Almost all of them old.

00:06:21.385 --> 00:06:24.685
One note said: 'Pension. Last savings.'

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:29.355
And at the bottom... your mother. With a smiley face.

00:06:31.655 --> 00:06:41.535
I love old people. They're polite. They trust a kind voice. And they say thank you... while you rob them.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:47.605
A whole university fund. Her birthday... my present.

00:06:50.005 --> 00:06:52.995
You didn't take a cent. You just showed everyone the truth.

00:06:53.595 --> 00:06:57.695
Every bank got the evidence. Every account in the chain froze.

00:06:58.695 --> 00:07:02.685
The police had hunted this gang for a year. Tonight, they got an address.

00:07:03.685 --> 00:07:05.825
And on forty screens... one message.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:12.265
Hello. You called my mother today.

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:14.175
Who is this?

00:07:15.275 --> 00:07:16.025
Her son.

00:07:17.025 --> 00:07:18.370
You should get the door.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.470
It's back. All of it!

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:31.700
What's back?

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.170
Nothing! Everything! Come here!

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.530
That morning, three hundred phones lit up across the country.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.900
Three hundred people got their savings back. And a little faith in people, too.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.780
You'd predicted every step. The arrests. The refunds.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:00.190
But not this. Three hundred strangers, laughing and crying at the same moment.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.420
Something better than you expected.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.870
And the spark finally lit up.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.870
Next year for my birthday... no phone calls, please.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.240
And for the first time in your life... you laughed right on time.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:20.230
That night, your computer turned on by itself. And someone started typing.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:38.890
Your whole life, nobody had ever been one step ahead of you. Until tonight.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.960
Finally. A real puzzle.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:48.630
So what would you do with five hundred IQ? Tell us in the comments.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:54.080
And if you loved that boss's last phone call... hit like, and subscribe for Part Two.

